Description: Fix NULL dereference on all-delimiter request buffers in
 validate_request()
 With --enable-command-args, the command name is tokenized with
 strtok(buff, "!"). A request whose buffer consists only of '!'
 separators (e.g. "!") makes strtok() return NULL, which is passed
 straight to strdup() -> NULL dereference -> the connection child
 crashes. Reachable by any host allowed by allowed_hosts; each
 malicious request kills its connection child (the parent survives,
 so this is a per-request crash / availability issue, not daemon
 death). Stock builds without --enable-command-args always use the
 non-NULL buff path and are unaffected.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- a/src/nrpe.c
+++ b/src/nrpe.c
@@ -2814,6 +2814,10 @@
 #else
 	ptr = buff;
 #endif
+	if (ptr == NULL) {
+		logit(LOG_ERR, "Error: Request contained no command name!");
+		return ERROR;
+	}
 	command_name = strdup(ptr);
 	if (command_name == NULL) {
 		logit(LOG_ERR, "Error: Memory allocation failed");
